simone biles is feeling the love i'm  excited  the 24 year old gymnast took to twitter  on wednesday to thank everyone for their  love and support  after withdrawing from the competitions  at the tokyo olympics  the outpouring of love and support i've  received has made me realize i'm more  than my accomplishments and gymnastics  which i never truly believed before  where we perform we're expected to win  which it can kind of get a lot at times  because we're so young with such  a big amount of pressure but i think we  handle it very well  on tuesday the athlete exited the  gymnastics team competition at the  summer olympics after the first rotation  then on wednesday morning it was  announced that she decided to withdraw  from the all-around competition as well  at the time the usa gymnastics team  tweeted quote  we wholeheartedly support simone's  decision and we applaud her bravery and  prioritizing her well-being  her courage shows yet again why she is a  role model for so many  everyone does strive to be the best and  we're such good friends that we're  rooting for each other no matter what  and we just want the best for each other  the statement also clarified that simone  will be quote  evaluated daily to determine whether or  not to participate in next week's  individual event finals where the  gymnastics superstar would be eligible  for more medals in the vault  uneven bars balance beam and floor  exercise  simone has a total of 30 olympic and  world championship medals  making her the most decorated american  gymnast  that is the ultimate goal and simone has  received a ton of love and support from  her fellow athletes and celebrities  praising her for putting her mental  health first  justin bieber posted a snap of the  olympian writing in part  quote nobody will ever understand the  pressures you face  i know we don't know each other but i'm  so proud of the decision to withdraw  michelle obama rhys witherspoon michael  phelps as well as simone's  boyfriend nfl pro jonathan owens also  expressed their support online  and simone's former dancing with the  stars pro sasha farber  told et he couldn't be more impressed  with simone  and her decision i feel so much  love for her she is such a hard worker  and i remember  um you know being in the gym with her  we had so much fun but there is just you  know this proves that she's human and  you know it's such a beautiful thing to  see i'm really thankful for that  the 24 year old standout athlete left  the competition floor during the team  finals on tuesday  after her first rotation on the vault  following her exit she spoke to the  today show  and gave a little insight into how she  was feeling physically i feel good i'm  in shape  emotionally that kind of varies on the  time in the moment you know  coming here to the olympics and being  the head  star of the olympics is not an easy feat  so we're just trying to take it one day  at a time and we'll see  she was ultimately replaced by alternate  jordan childs  and the team went on to win the silver  medal i'm super proud of these girls  that stepped up and did what they needed  to do and now we're  olympic silver medalist so it's  something that they'll cherish forever  after being awarded her silver medal  simone shared  this snap of her team on instagram  writing quote  olympic silver medalists i'm so proud of  these girls right here  you girls are incredibly brave and  talented i'll forever be inspired by  your determination to not give up and to  fight through adversity  they stepped up when i couldn't thanks  for being there for me and having my  back  forever love y'all  [Music]
 

